      "content": "Evolutionary search loops around language models can solve optimization problems that stump single-pass reasoning.\n\nAlphaEvolve pairs generative code suggestions from large language models with automated evaluators in an iterative evolutionary cycle. Instead of relying on a single chain of thought, the system generates candidate algorithms, evaluates them against verification harnesses, and mutates successful candidates across generations.\n\nIn a benchmark spanning 67 open problems across combinatorics, geometry, and number theory, this approach rediscovered known bounds and established strictly improved solutions in several cases. The framework also interfaces directly with formal proof systems like AlphaProof to turn discovered constructions into verified mathematical arguments.\n\nFor systems engineers designing autonomous agents, this highlights a critical architectural pattern. Scaling the verification harness and feedback loop yields far better results than merely increasing model parameter size.\n\nReliable verification turns uncertain model generation into deterministic discovery."
